  "body": "Found during the 2026-11-07 fleet-wide DB audit + rename/mode-fix program (#6619).\n\nFacts, all empirically verified on scratch DBs (CLI v1.0.33):\n- `turso db list` TYPE column is the only mode evidence: `SQLite` = libsql mode, `Turso` = TursoDB mode.\n- There is no `turso db rename`.\n- A `--from-db` fork INHERITS the source database's type; `turso db create --from-db X --tursodb` fails with \"tursodb flag contradicts the database derived type\". A fork can never change mode.\n- The only working conversion is: `turso db export <db>` -> copy the export files to the target basename -> `turso db import <file>.db --tursodb` (the new DB is named after the FILE basename), then repoint every producer, confirm, and delete the old DB.\n- `turso db dump` does not exist in this CLI version (prints help).\n\nImpact: converting the fleet's 8 libsql DBs on 2026-11-07 meant 8 full data moves (~7.7 GB total exports), per-DB token re-mints, and producer flips — for what should be a metadata operation. If Turso ever ships a mode-convert or rename verb, the fleet's remaining libsql holdouts (atlas monolith, great-star-lord — both deliberately untouched, see #6619) should use it. Until then, any new fleet DB must be created with --tursodb at birth; a libsql DB created by accident costs a full migration later.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The rule 'every new fleet Turso DB is created with --tursodb at birth' is recorded in the fleet's DB-creation documentation/runbook where a creator will see it.\n- [ ] The remaining libsql holdouts named in the issue (atlas monolith, great-star-lord) are listed as known conversion debt with the export/import conversion procedure linked.\n- [ ] If/when Turso ships a rename or mode-convert verb, the holdouts are converted with it and this issue is closed citing that conversion; until then this issue stays as the tracking record, not active work.\n",
